On Thursday 03 March 2011 11:15:09 Ian Johnson wrote:
> Why is {no'a ra'o} not silly?

Here's my standard example:
la djan. klama le zdani be vo'a pu le nu la meris. no'a = John went to his 
house before Mary did. (Mary went to John's house.)
la djan. klama le zdani be vo'a pu le nu la meris. no'a ra'o = John went home 
before Mary did. (Mary went to her own house.)

Pierre
-- 
Jews use a lunisolar calendar; Muslims use a solely lunar calendar.

